From 555e9efb0e84e0d13d857d0955e9b6366dbdb89d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: homelab <homelab@emrys.dev>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 21:15:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/10] build: overlay context for the in-cluster builder

The cluster builder delivers its context as a ConfigMap: only top-level files
are copied and the whole thing is capped near 900 KB. This repository is
~14 MB with the app in subdirectories, so its own Dockerfile cannot be built
there.

homelab-image/ pins the upstream 1.55.3 image by digest and copies exactly the
six files this series changes or adds. make-context.sh stages them flat from
the checkout and prints their sha256, so the built image is traceable to the
tree that was tested without a second copy of the source in git.

The README records the base-image check: all 293 files in the upstream image
are byte-identical to a pristine git archive of tag 1.55.3, so any difference
in the result comes from the overlay.
