+# A patch-overlay image: the upstream release, plus this fork's changed files.
+#
+# WHY NOT build the repository's own Dockerfile: the cluster builder
+# (scripts/build-image.sh) delivers its context as a ConfigMap with two hard
+# properties - only TOP-LEVEL files are copied, and the whole thing is capped
+# at 1 MiB. This repository is ~14 MB across app.py plus routes/, services/,
+# templates/ and Database/, so its own Dockerfile cannot be built there
+# without changing the builder. An overlay is small, reproducible, and states
+# exactly which files differ from upstream.
+#
+# THE BASE IS PINNED BY DIGEST, not by tag, for the same reason the live
+# Deployment is: a repushed tag must not silently change what this fork runs
+# on. The digest below is the multi-arch index for upstream 1.55.3, the
+# version this patch series was written against and the one deployed.
+#
+# THE CONTEXT IS GENERATED. `make-context.sh` copies the changed files out of
+# the checkout into .context/ under flat names (the ConfigMap would drop the
+# subdirectories), with this Dockerfile. Build with:
+#
+#   homelab/scripts/dev/dev-build.sh spotifystatstracker \
+#     --context homelab-image/.context --image spotify-tracker:1.55.3-homelab.1
+#
+# `homelab-image/README.md` records how the base was verified against tag
+# 1.55.3 and how to check the result.
+FROM docker.io/i7gamer/spotify-tracker:1.55.3@sha256:79b40166b07376de7d2646272eaa0e7b9578c5512e59c464f65a544545e12b30
+
+# Each COPY overwrites one file that exists in the base; nothing is added to a
+# path the app does not already read. Flat source names are a builder
+# constraint (see above), not a design choice.
+COPY app.py /app/app.py
+COPY config.py /app/config.py
+COPY auth.py /app/routes/auth.py
+COPY trusted_header_route.py /app/routes/trusted_header.py
+COPY trusted_header_service.py /app/services/trusted_header.py
+COPY connect_spotify.html /app/templates/connect_spotify.html
diff --git a/homelab-image/README.md b/homelab-image/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..6b14551
--- /dev/null
+++ b/homelab-image/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,72 @@
+# homelab-image: the patch-overlay build
+
+This directory is how the fork is built in-cluster, and it exists because the
+builder cannot take this repository's own Dockerfile.
+
+## Why an overlay
+
+`homelab/scripts/build-image.sh` turns its build context into a ConfigMap with
+`kubectl create configmap --from-file=DIR`. Two consequences are load-bearing:
+
+* **Only top-level files are copied.** Subdirectories are silently skipped.
+  This repository is ~14 MB across `routes/`, `services/`, `templates/`,
+  `Database/` and `static/`, so copying the checkout would build an image
+  missing almost all of the app.
+* **The context is capped at ~900 KB** by the script's own guard (the
+  ConfigMap's 1 MiB limit). Even a tar of the source is larger.
+
+The overlay avoids both: the base is the upstream release image, pinned by
+digest, and the context is six flat files that replace or add exactly the
+files this patch series changed. `make-context.sh` stages them from the
+checkout, so there is no second copy to drift.
+
+## Build
+
+```sh
+# from the checkout root, in the dev environment
+homelab-image/make-context.sh
+~/homelab/scripts/dev/dev-build.sh spotifystatstracker \
+  --context homelab-image/.context \
+  --image registry.emrys.dev/homelab/spotify-tracker:1.55.3-homelab.1
+```
+
+`make-context.sh` prints a sha256 for every source file; the same values are
+written to `patched-files.txt` in the context.
+
+## Why the base digest is trusted
+
+The `FROM` line is pinned to the multi-arch index for upstream **1.55.3** - the
+version the live deployment runs and the version this patch series was written
+against. Before the first patched build, the base image was verified against a
+pristine `git archive 1.55.3` checkout:
+
+```text
+files in the image (excluding __pycache__): 293
+files compared with tag 1.55.3:              293
+files differing:                               0
+files in the image with no tag counterpart:    0
+```
+
+Every file the image ships is byte-identical to the tag; the remaining tag
+files are excluded by the repository's `.dockerignore` (tests, docs, dev
+tooling). So a change in the built image can only come from the overlay.
+
+After a build, the same comparison can be run against the result: all files
+except the six below must be identical to the base, and the six must match
+`patched-files.txt`:
+
+| Context file | Destination in the image | Change |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `app.py` | `/app/app.py` | trusted-header init, request path, cookie verification |
+| `config.py` | `/app/config.py` | the two settings and the session key |
+| `auth.py` | `/app/routes/auth.py` | cookie verification delegated to the shared helper |
+| `trusted_header_route.py` | `/app/routes/trusted_header.py` | new: the hook and `/connect-spotify` |
+| `trusted_header_service.py` | `/app/services/trusted_header.py` | new: settings parsing, peer check, identity |
+| `connect_spotify.html` | `/app/templates/connect_spotify.html` | new: the cookie page |
+
+## What the next patch should not assume
+
+This path works because the overlay is small. A change that adds a static
+asset, a migration file or a new package would need either a bigger context or
+a different builder input (a tar/OCI context or a git fetch in the build Job).
+The real fix belongs in `scripts/build-image.sh`, not in a larger overlay.
diff --git a/homelab-image/make-context.sh b/homelab-image/make-context.sh
new file mode 100755
index 0000000..94244c6
--- /dev/null
+++ b/homelab-image/make-context.sh
@@ -0,0 +1,40 @@
+#!/usr/bin/env bash
+# Stage the flat build context for homelab-image/Dockerfile.
+#
+# WHY FLAT: scripts/build-image.sh turns the context into a ConfigMap with
+# `kubectl create configmap --from-file=DIR`, which copies only the files at
+# the top level (subdirectories are silently dropped) and caps the whole thing
+# at 1 MiB. The repository is ~14 MB and mostly subdirectories, so the context
+# is a generated directory of renamed files instead of the checkout.
+#
+# THE SOURCE IS THE CHECKOUT. Every copied file is read from this repository,
+# so the image is the working tree that was tested - not a second copy that can
+# drift. The manifest this writes names every file and its sha256; compare it
+# with `sha256sum` in the built image to prove the overlay landed.
+set -euo pipefail
+
+here="$(CDPATH= cd -- "$(dirname -- "$0")" && pwd)"
+root="$(CDPATH= cd -- "$here/.." && pwd)"
+ctx="$here/.context"
+
+rm -rf "$ctx"
+mkdir -p "$ctx"
+
+copy() {  # <source relative to repo root> <flat name in the context>
+  local source="$root/$1" name="$2"
+  [ -f "$source" ] || { echo "make-context: missing $1" >&2; exit 1; }
+  cp "$source" "$ctx/$name"
+  printf '%s  %s\n' "$(sha256sum "$source" | cut -d' ' -f1)" "$1" >> "$ctx/patched-files.txt"
+}
+
+: > "$ctx/patched-files.txt"
+copy app.py app.py
+copy config.py config.py
+copy routes/auth.py auth.py
+copy routes/trusted_header.py trusted_header_route.py
+copy services/trusted_header.py trusted_header_service.py
+copy templates/connect_spotify.html connect_spotify.html
+cp "$here/Dockerfile" "$ctx/Dockerfile"
+
+echo "make-context: staged $ctx"
+cat "$ctx/patched-files.txt"
-- 
